1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,099
You type a question into

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,519
ChatGPT, and a second later

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,499
an answer starts appearing, word

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:06,100
by word.

5
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,980
But where is it coming from?

6
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,840
There's no person typing.

7
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,060
It isn't copying a web page.

8
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:14,379
Most of the time, it isn't

9
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,580
looking anything up at all.

10
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,779
So where does the answer come

11
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:18,100
from?

12
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,459
Quick test, finish this sentence

13
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:22,680
Once upon a…

14
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,340
You said time, didn't you?

15
00:00:27,033 --> 00:00:28,492
then you just did exactly what

16
00:00:28,493 --> 00:00:29,653
ChatGPT does.

17
00:00:30,793 --> 00:00:32,673
ChatGPT is a guessing machine.

18
00:00:33,213 --> 00:00:35,112
It looks at the word so far and

19
00:00:35,113 --> 00:00:36,632
guesses the most likely next

20
00:00:36,633 --> 00:00:36,893
word.

21
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:39,293
It adds that word, looks again,

22
00:00:39,553 --> 00:00:41,472
and guesses the next one, and

23
00:00:41,473 --> 00:00:41,893
the next.

24
00:00:42,973 --> 00:00:43,653
That's it.

25
00:00:44,373 --> 00:00:45,772
Every answer it has ever given

26
00:00:45,773 --> 00:00:47,552
you was built like that, one

27
00:00:47,553 --> 00:00:48,413
guess at a time.

28
00:00:49,353 --> 00:00:50,393
So three questions.

29
00:00:51,233 --> 00:00:52,013
Guessing from what?

30
00:00:52,653 --> 00:00:53,852
Why can't it count letters?

31
00:00:53,853 --> 00:00:55,972
And why does the same question

32
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:56,973
get different answers?

33
00:00:57,733 --> 00:00:59,272
Question one, guessing from

34
00:00:59,273 --> 00:00:59,553
what?

35
00:01:00,173 --> 00:01:01,792
You knew time because you've

36
00:01:01,793 --> 00:01:03,353
heard that line 100 times.

37
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:05,853
ChatGPT learned the same way,

38
00:01:06,153 --> 00:01:07,413
just on a giant scale.

39
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:09,532
Remember, fill in the blank

40
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:10,593
worksheets from school.

41
00:01:11,293 --> 00:01:12,313
The cat sat on the blank.

42
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:13,793
That's its training.

43
00:01:14,493 --> 00:01:16,013
It was shown a mountain of text,

44
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:18,372
books, websites, articles, with

45
00:01:18,373 --> 00:01:19,293
the next word hidden.

46
00:01:19,873 --> 00:01:20,353
It guessed.

47
00:01:21,033 --> 00:01:22,013
The guess was checked.

48
00:01:22,653 --> 00:01:24,332
If it was wrong, it got adjusted

49
00:01:24,333 --> 00:01:25,133
a tiny bit.

50
00:01:25,663 --> 00:01:27,993
Then again, billions of times.

51
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:30,553
Nobody gave it a list of facts.

52
00:01:31,193 --> 00:01:32,712
It just got incredibly good at

53
00:01:32,713 --> 00:01:33,033
blanks.

54
00:01:33,693 --> 00:01:35,452
That's why this kind of AI is

55
00:01:35,453 --> 00:01:36,573
called a language model.

56
00:01:37,233 --> 00:01:38,672
Then people trained it some more

57
00:01:38,673 --> 00:01:39,912
to answer like a helpful

58
00:01:39,913 --> 00:01:40,373
assistant.

59
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:42,652
But underneath, it's still the

60
00:01:42,653 --> 00:01:43,992
world's best fill in the blank

61
00:01:43,993 --> 00:01:44,293
player.

62
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,279
Question two, how many R's are

63
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:47,820
in strawberry?

64
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,320
Three, but for a long time,

65
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:53,459
ChatGPT would confidently say

66
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:54,140
two.

67
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:55,860
Here's why.

68
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:57,879
I've been saying it guesses the

69
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:58,460
next word.

70
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:00,340
That was a little white lie.

71
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:02,600
It doesn't see words or letters.

72
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,780
It sees chunks called tokens.

73
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,079
Your message gets chopped into

74
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:09,259
pieces and each piece becomes a

75
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:09,480
number.

76
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,679
Strawberry might get chopped

77
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:13,180
into three pieces like this.

78
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,679
Now imagine I text you a

79
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,739
strawberry emoji and ask how

80
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:18,820
many R's are in it.

81
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,479
The picture doesn't show any

82
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:20,780
letters.

83
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:22,579
You'd have to remember the

84
00:02:22,580 --> 00:02:22,920
spelling.

85
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,140
That's ChatGPT's problem.

86
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,639
Newer versions usually work

87
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:29,039
around it by spelling the word

88
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:29,600
out first.

89
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:31,460
But the chunks are still there,

90
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,339
so letter puzzles can still trip

91
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:33,640
it up.

92
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,399
Question three, ask the same

93
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,359
question twice and you'll often

94
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,580
get two different answers.

95
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:40,520
Why?

96
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:42,619
Because it doesn't always pick

97
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:43,680
the single top guess.

98
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:45,739
Think about your favorite

99
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:46,380
restaurant.

100
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,900
Most days you order your usual.

101
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,179
Some days you try the dish you

102
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:51,920
almost ordered.

103
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:53,999
The setting that controls this

104
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,100
is called temperature.

105
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,099
Turn it down and it orders the

106
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,660
usual every single time.

107
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,400
Safe but a bit boring.

108
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,279
Turn it up and it gets

109
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:03,820
adventurous.

110
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,619
More creative and too far up it

111
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:07,680
starts ordering nonsense.

112
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,359
ChatGPT keeps it turned up a

113
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:10,500
little.

114
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,359
And once one word changes, every

115
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,820
guess after it changes too.

116
00:03:15,467 --> 00:03:16,607
So put it all together.

117
00:03:17,347 --> 00:03:18,906
Your message gets chopped into

118
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:19,387
tokens.

119
00:03:20,307 --> 00:03:22,066
ChatGPT guesses the next one

120
00:03:22,067 --> 00:03:23,866
from patterns in a mountain of

121
00:03:23,867 --> 00:03:24,227
text.

122
00:03:24,987 --> 00:03:25,926
Picks one with a little

123
00:03:25,927 --> 00:03:26,567
randomness.

124
00:03:27,327 --> 00:03:29,267
Adds it and guesses again.

125
00:03:30,307 --> 00:03:31,646
There's no finished answer

126
00:03:31,647 --> 00:03:32,447
waiting somewhere.

127
00:03:32,887 --> 00:03:34,547
It's built one guess at a time,

128
00:03:34,807 --> 00:03:36,026
the same way you finished

129
00:03:36,027 --> 00:03:37,027
Once upon a.

130
00:03:37,827 --> 00:03:39,307
And notice what it's guessing.

131
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:43,066
What sounds right, not what is

132
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:43,387
right.

133
00:03:44,287 --> 00:03:46,166
Most of the time, those are the

134
00:03:46,167 --> 00:03:46,707
same thing.

135
00:03:47,367 --> 00:03:48,687
But sometimes they're not.

136
00:03:49,307 --> 00:03:50,626
And that's when AI makes

137
00:03:50,627 --> 00:03:51,986
something up, with total

138
00:03:51,987 --> 00:03:52,507
confidence.

139
00:03:53,227 --> 00:03:54,966
It's called a hallucination, and

140
00:03:54,967 --> 00:03:55,467
it's next.

141
00:03:57,007 --> 00:03:58,426
Subscribe so you don't miss why

142
00:03:58,427 --> 00:03:59,687
AI hallucinates.

143
00:04:00,207 --> 00:04:01,367
And tell me in the comments,

144
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:03,866
what's the strangest thing an AI

145
00:04:03,867 --> 00:04:04,947
has ever told you?
